# Findings

### CX-DC-01 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: Wave-1 arrival agreement audit and shuffled-index gate are absent

The arrival preflight explicitly says agreement is “a later cut” and returns no agreement verdict: [preflight.py:381](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/preflight.py:381). `canonical_audit.py` remains the legacy JSONL byte-offset/count/last-line and rowid-order audit: [canonical_audit.py:1](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/canonical_audit.py:1), [canonical_audit.py:316](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/canonical_audit.py:316), [canonical_audit.py:548](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/canonical_audit.py:548). There is no slice-D gate directory.

Contradicted design sentence: “`canonical_audit.py`’s entire offset/prefix custody model moves to arrival … [and] audit vectors over a deliberately rebuilt and shuffled index” ([Plan §3D](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:79), [gate](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:83)).

### CX-DC-02 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: public witness positions remain projection rowids

`WitnessPosition` stores `fact_id`, `rowid`, `seq`, lineage and store path; its prefix is `WHERE rowid <= rowid`: [witness.py:164](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/witness.py:164). Same-lineage portability is implemented by resolving the fact id to another projection’s rowid: [witness.py:471](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/witness.py:471). The r1 Law-4 fix makes misuse structural, but it does not re-key the coordinate.

Contradicted design sentences: “Its position is the witness position: `(arrival_lineage, ordinal)`” ([Substrate §3](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:92)); “witness addressing, re-keyed on `(lineage, ordinal)`” ([Substrate §9](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:471)); and Plan D’s seal/witness rebase ([Plan §3D](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:79)).

### CX-DC-03 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: seals remain derived-index rowid commitments

Window bounds are fact ids but resolve to SQLite rowids: [sqlite_store.py:1531](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1531). Window membership and order are selected by `rowid`: [sqlite_store.py:1547](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1547). New tick state takes its cursor and predecessor from SQLite projection rows: [sqlite_store.py:1622](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1622).

Contradicted design sentence: “seals, chain verification, signing — re-based on arrival positions” ([Substrate §9](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:477)); Plan D is more explicit: “Seals re-base on `(arrival_lineage, ordinal)`” ([Plan §3D](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:79)).

### CX-DC-04 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: the three-movement genesis is not an admission precondition

`ArrivalLog.mint` publishes after writing only the structural genesis: [arrival.py:753](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival.py:753). Normal append is immediately available: [arrival.py:1264](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival.py:1264). The ratified authority gate itself demonstrates ordinary records at ordinals 1 and 3, declaration absorption at 4, and the first seal at 5: [test_arrival_authority_gate.py:62](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_authority_gate.py:62).

Contradicted design sentence: “A fresh 1.0 log opens with a genesis ceremony of three movements — self-certifying genesis, declaration absorption, seal — committed before the first ordinary admission” ([Log §5](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/2-the-arrival-log.md:201)). The later ratified A proposal repeats the same order: [slice-A proposal:116](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/dev/arrival-sliceA-authority-design-2026-08-18.md:116).

### CX-DC-05 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: declaration ceremonies also guard the everything-head

The public token is correctly declaration-scoped, but `_ceremony_persist` passes the reconciled overall arrival ordinal as `following`, so any intervening record refuses the append: [arrival_store.py:462](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/arrival_store.py:462). A test explicitly pins refusal when an ordinary interloper lands: [test_arrival_store.py:385](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/tests/test_arrival_store.py:385).

Contradicted design sentence: “CAS against the arrival head would be spuriously strict: any ordinary admission between fold-out and re-absorb would fail an edit with no actual conflict” ([Log §9](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/2-the-arrival-log.md:346)). The later C ruling says the lineage-filtered `_decl.*` predicate is preserved verbatim: [C Q3](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-sliceC/design-proposal.md:57).

### CX-DC-06 — SILENT-DIVERGENCE: standing aggregation membership is still file/path authority

The declaration loader openly reports aggregate membership as current-file state because aggregation tables are not built: [declaration.py:440](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/declaration.py:440). Store resolution still consumes `combine`/`discover` paths: [vertex_reader.py:120](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/vertex_reader.py:120). Although `_decl.member-defined` documents exist, the grammar forbids `combine` together with a store, so a standing combine cannot absorb them into its own lineage: [loader.py:858](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/loader.py:858).

Contradicted design sentence: “Membership … [is] declaration state, changed through the declaration ceremony in the aggregator’s own log,” while the discover glob “degrades from authority to a discovery driver” ([Log §8](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/2-the-arrival-log.md:306), [Log §8 table](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/2-the-arrival-log.md:322)).

### CX-DC-07 — DESIGN-DEBT: the Substrate overstates rowid’s cryptographic role

The Substrate says “window hashes, cursors” are computed over rowid ranges and that cryptographic commitments rest on rowid: [Substrate §2](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:76). The code’s signed tick envelope contains fact-id cursors, not rowids: [sqlite_store.py:158](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:158). Rowid is only the local selector used after resolving those ids: [sqlite_store.py:1531](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:1531).

The Log itself corrects this claim: “no rowid was ever inside signed or hashed bytes” ([Log §10](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/2-the-arrival-log.md:407)).

### CX-DC-08 — DESIGN-DEBT: PR #8’s combined-read receipt still calls the ruled state open

The implementation now resolves aggregate ordering through `ByKey`, defaulting to `ByKey("ts")`, and structurally refuses aggregate `Arrival`: [vertex_reader.py:397](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/engine/src/engine/vertex_reader.py:397). But the carried PR #8 receipt still labels R2 an “interim state” and says the question “needs a ruling”: [RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md:69](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md:69), [RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md:177](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/RECEIPT_ORDER_FOLD.md:177).

Contradicted design sentence: “Combined-read fold fork → declared projection ordering” ([Plan §6](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/3-the-arrival-plan.md:113)). `decision:design/arrival-sliceC-ordering` expressly said the interim comment and R2/R3 residue retire.

### CX-DC-09 — DESIGN-DEBT: the Substrate’s decomposition status is stale

The Substrate says: “The four cuts have not been attacked as a decomposition — nobody has pressure-tested whether cut A is atomically shippable” ([Substrate §11](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/scratch/arrival-branch-review/design-artifacts/1-the-arrival-substrate.md:529)).

